cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SafeGraphs: A Portable, Memory-Mappable Format for Exchanging Proximity Graphs"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/safegraphs/SafeGraphs
abstract: >-
  SafeGraphs is a simple format for exchanging graph-shaped search indexes between CPUs, GPUs and
  machines, serving as an interoperability layer between NSW, CAGRA and similar nearest-neighbor
  algorithms. A graph is exchanged through its keys, values and neighbor lists alone, with no
  knowledge of how it was built or how it will be searched, and files stay memory-mappable so that
  indexes built on large GPU machines remain usable on consumer hardware. It absorbs new element
  types, from mixed-precision floats to variable-length and sparse payloads, without breaking
  readability, while each application chooses its own scoring and traversal.
keywords:
  - proximity graph
  - nearest-neighbor search
  - file format
  - interoperability
  - memory mapping
  - vector search
  - gpu

authors:
  - family-names: Vardanian
    given-names: Ash
    alias: ashvardanian
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4882-1815
